23 0 obj
<< /A 614 0 R /Alt (Flowchart diagram outlining patient selection and analysis steps for a study. Cases meeting diagnostic criteria are divided into groups based on IgAV, appendicitis, and intussusception, with exclusions detailed. Resulting groups are separated into training and validation datasets, with further steps including missing-data imputation, variable selection using LASSO regression plus BIC, logistic regression model, nomogram creation, five-fold cross-validation, model evaluation with ROC and calibration curve, and sensitivity and subgroup analyses.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 16 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 615 0 R /Alt (Table and forest plot summarizing a multivariate logistic regression analysis of clinical variables, displaying odds ratios with 95 percent confidence intervals. Statistically significant variables include age, fever, nausea or vomiting, symptom duration, borborygmi patterns, monocyte and platelet counts, mean platelet volume, and albumin, with odds ratios visually distinguished by colored diamonds and confidence bars.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 19 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 616 0 R /Alt (Four-panel figure displaying model performance metrics. Panel A is an ROC curve comparing cross-validation \(AUC 0.958\) and validation dataset \(AUC 0.992\); Panel B is a calibration curve showing observed versus predicted probabilities for both datasets; Panel C is a decision curve analysis plotting net benefit by threshold probability; Panel D is a clinical impact curve comparison showing number of high-risk patients and those with events by threshold probability for both datasets.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 19 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
26 0 obj
<< /A 617 0 R /Alt (Nomogram graphic depicting variables for a clinical prediction model, including age, fever, nausea or vomiting, symptom onset time, borborygmi activity, blood counts, mean platelet volume, and albumin, mapping to total points and predicted probability.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 20 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
